    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d655">

                <pb facs="0782" n="670" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg670"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1111 Stam, John C/47: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-02-05T18:00:00-05:00">February 5, 1935—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>35. Your 26, January 17, 8 p.m. and despatch No. 3234, January 4,<anchor n="80"
                        xml:id="d655-f1"/> the last received. Please send by naval radio a summary
                    of the steps taken and the results attained to date by the Chinese Government as
                    a consequence of the Stam murder and a statement of the Legation’s opinion
                    whether the action taken by the Chinese Government is all that might reasonably
                    be expected in the circumstances. Has the Chinese Government given any
                    acceptable assurances that any persons connected with the murder have been
                    punished?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d655-f1" n="80" xml:id="d655-f1-content">
